Ollama Docker Setup — Models & Customization Guide

---

OVERVIEW

This setup runs a local Ollama inference server with a Web UI and an automated model builder.

It does NOT download models automatically.

Instead:

* You provide base models manually
* The system generates customized variants from them

---

MODEL STORAGE (IMPORTANT)

Base models are read from:

/home/${LINUX_USERNAME}/.ollama

This is the default Ollama directory on Linux.

Key points:

* This directory is shared with the container
* It is expected to already contain models
* If empty → NO models will be available
* The system cannot download models by itself

How to add models:

Option 1 (recommended):

* Run locally:
  ollama pull llama3:8b

Option 2:

* Manually place models into ~/.ollama

---

CUSTOM MODELS (MODFILES)

Custom models are generated from base models using Modelfiles.

Location:

./modelfiles/

Structure:

modelfiles/
└── <base_model[:tag]>/
├── Modelfile-<custom_name>
└── ...

Example:

modelfiles/
└── llama3:8b/
├── Modelfile-assistant
├── Modelfile-coder

Each Modelfile defines how to modify the base model:

* system prompt
* parameters
* behavior tuning

---

NAMING

Each generated model follows:

<base_name>-<tag>-<custom_name>

Example:

llama3-8b-assistant
llama3-8b-coder

---

MODEL BUILD PROCESS

Handled by: model-loader container

At startup:

1. Scan /modelfiles
2. For each base model:

   * Check if it exists
   * If missing → attempt to pull
3. For each Modelfile:

   * Create derived model via:
     ollama create

This runs automatically on container start.

---

INFERENCE FLOW

Once running:

open-webui → sends prompt → ollama → model generates response

* ollama = inference server
* models = used at runtime
* custom variants behave according to Modelfiles

---

DOCKER SERVICES

ollama:

* Core inference engine
* Uses GPU if available
* Stores models in ~/.ollama

open-webui:

* Accessible UI (port 3000)
* Connects to ollama

model-loader:

* One-shot setup container
* Builds all custom models

---

⚠️ CRITICAL WARNING

The directory:

/home/${LINUX_USERNAME}/.ollama

CANNOT be mounted as read-only.

Reason:

* Ollama requires write access to create derived models

Implication:

* The container CAN modify your local models
* Treat this directory as sensitive

Recommendation:

* Do NOT manually edit files inside
* Do NOT run untrusted Modelfiles
* Consider backups if important

---

LIMITATION

Ollama currently:

* Does NOT allow custom model storage paths
* Forces use of ~/.ollama

This is why the setup must use that directory.

---

ADDING A NEW CUSTOM MODEL

1. Ensure base model exists:
   ollama pull mistral:7b

2. Create directory:
   modelfiles/mistral:7b/

3. Add file:
   Modelfile-chat

4. Restart:
   docker compose up -d

5. Use:
   mistral-7b-chat

---

DEBUGGING

List models:
ollama list

Check builder logs:
docker logs model-loader

Rebuild manually:
ollama create <name> -f <Modelfile>

---

MODEL SOURCES

Official library:
https://ollama.com/library

Alternative models:
https://huggingface.co/

(Compatibility may vary)

---

SUMMARY

* You provide base models manually
* The system generates custom variants automatically
* Everything runs locally
* ~/.ollama is the single source of truth

